To send PGP encrypted emails in Thunderbird, set up OpenPGP, generate your key pair, import the recipient's public key, and then compose and encrypt your message before sending.
Step-by-Step Instructions
Set Up Thunderbird:
Ensure you have Thunderbird version 78 or higher, as it includes built-in support for OpenPGP encryption. If you haven't installed it yet, download it from the official Thunderbird website. 
