Create Your OpenPGP Key Pair:
Open Thunderbird and go to Account Settings by clicking the menu button (three horizontal lines) and selecting Account Settings.
Click on End-to-End Encryption in the left pane, then click Add Key.
Choose Create a new OpenPGP Key and follow the prompts to generate your key pair. You can set an expiration date for better key hygiene. 
2


2 Sources
Import the Recipient's Public Key:
Obtain the public key of the recipient you wish to send an encrypted email to. This key must be imported into Thunderbird.
In the End-to-End Encryption settings, click on OpenPGP Manager, then select File > Import Public Keys from File to import the recipient's public key. 
2


2 Sources
Compose Your Email:
Start a new email by clicking Write in Thunderbird.
In the compose window, enter the recipient's email address (whose public key you imported) and write your message.
Encrypt the Email:
Before sending, look for the OpenPGP drop-down menu in the compose window. Select Encrypt to encrypt your email. You can also click the Encrypt button at the bottom right of the compose window. 
2
If the recipient has the matching private key, they will be able to decrypt and read your email. 
