Additional Notes
Understanding Keys: Your public key is shared with others to allow them to send you encrypted messages, while your private key is kept secret and used to decrypt messages sent to you. 
1
Digital Signatures: You can also digitally sign your emails to verify your identity to the recipient, ensuring the message hasn't been altered in transit. 
